WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.030
The summer sun sure feels nice, doesn't it?

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.140
Yep!

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.940
The flowerbeds seem to be doing well in all this sunlight too.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.030
Some of them don't seem to be.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.160
Oh! These are the Gardening Club president, Mizushima Aya's...

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.160
Marigolds

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.160
Mizushima Aya

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.160
Gardening Club

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.940
The Gardening Club? Oh, I see!

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.190
So this section of the grounds is for the Gardening Club's flower beds.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.540
Th-This isn't good!

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.340
What's the matter?

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.990
I completely forgot to go to the Gardening Club !

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.460
What?! How much have you missed?!

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.210
All of yesterday.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.390
Just a day?

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.320
Wait...

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.430
When did you join the Gardening Club?

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:43.040
{OP}

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.230
HeartCatch

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.690
Precure!

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.240
HeartCatch Precure!

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.240
Now, all together

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.750
HeartCatch Precure!

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.710
Let's make our flowers bloom

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.330
Within each of our chests,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.000
they begin to sprout

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.670
The seeds of the heart

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.970
are growing

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.600
bit by bit

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:16.260
Red,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:16.890
white

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.180
and yellow

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.930
It's because these blooming buds are

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.350
all varied colors

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:23.810
that they

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.020
shine so brightly!

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:31.320
That smile that you've nurtured

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.820
with such care

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.530
will never wither

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.120
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.000
Now, all together

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.500
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:48.170
Let's make our flowers bloom!

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:53.050
They're always right by our sides

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:53.880
So together

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.720
let's make those pretty flowers of our heart

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.680
bloom even more!

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.180
HeartCatch

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.680
Precure!

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.900
And so, I'll be attending the Gardening Club today.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.980
Then I'm coming with you.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.320
Huh? Why?

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.060
You're the Fashion Club's precious vice president!

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.910
As president, I need to introduce myself too, don't I?

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.040
I need to warn them what'll happen if they try to steal you away.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:33.250
Nothing, nothing! I didn't say a thing!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.090
Oh! They're sure working hard!

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.640
The girl carrying the soil must be... a first-year?

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:48.140
No, that's the club president, Mizushima Aya!

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.340
Huh?! The president?!

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:58.820
We've Finally Found You<i>!</i>

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:58.820
We've Finally Found You<i>!</i>

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.990
Hey, Aya.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:01.940
Huh?

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.790
Please stop, President!

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.410
It's not that simple!

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.850
The flowers...

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.630
Are you all right?!

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:24.150
Because I'm such a klutz, our precious flowers are ruined...

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.530
Don't cry, President!

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.850
I'm sorry. It's my fault for calling out to you so suddenly.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.900
No. It's not your fault, Hanasaki.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:41.300
Um, I just wanted to say that I'm sorry for not coming to club yesterday!

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.450
You're apologizing to me just because you missed one day?

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.330
You're so brilliant, Hanasaki...

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.020
Um... she's crying again.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.540
You mustn't cry, President!

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:02.380
Please excuse me. I can get rather emotional at times.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.560
By the way, who's this?

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.650
The president of the Fashion Club that Tsubomi's vice president of...

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.270
Kurumi Erika!

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.350
It's very nice to meet you!

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.060
She's kinda scary.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.980
A-Aya, were you carrying that soil over to use in the flowerbeds?

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.650
Th-That's right.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.280
Marigolds

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.280
Mizushima Aya

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.280
Gardening Club

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:27.360
The flowers aren't doing too well, so I thought
 I'd change the amount of fertilizer we're using.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.030
Mister flower, are you not feeling too well?

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.580
Try to get better soon, okay?

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:40.380
When you talk to the flowers, Hanasaki, it makes me feel like they'll get better. {they will -> they'll to improve flow}

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.670
Don't be silly.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.630
But your flowers always seem to do so well.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.810
Hanasaki, do you have a green thumb?

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.760
A green thumb?

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:56.470
That's what you call people with a natural affinity for raising flowers!

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.900
No way! I couldn't have one!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.530
No, I think you might.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.740
After all, you're the granddaughter of a botanical gardener!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.410
Huh?! You mean the famous botanical scientist, Professor Hanasaki Kaoruko?!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.490
Y-Yeah...

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.250
That's amazing! Please, can you 
introduce me to Professor Kaoruko?!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:14.790
Huh?

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:20.000
I'm the president of the Gardening Club, and yet I'm so terrible at raising flowers.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.080
It's more like they wilt just from me touching them.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.780
That's why she decided to just
 focus on mixing the soil today.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:32.810
That's why I want to ask Professor Kaoruko's opinion on what I'm doing wrong!

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.020
In that case, it shouldn't be a problem.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.020
I'm... I'm so happy...

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.220
Let's go!

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:40.860
Huh?

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:50.910
But first, I need to clean up all that soil I spilled! {spilt -> spilled, a little too British here wot wot.}

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:55.960
Ah! Why do I have to be such a scatterbrain?!

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.000
Get a grip, President!

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.840
Jusht where could the third Precure be?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.190
There's no need to get so flustered!

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:07.500
I'm sure the new Precure will appear sooner or later.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.280
I'm sure they will too.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:10.010
Huh?

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.220
Grandma!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.220
And I'm sure, when you find them, you'll sense something special about them.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.520
Shense shomething?

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.620
Indeed.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.520
Hey, Tsubomi's grandma!

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.230
Why, if it isn't Erika.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:27.140
Today we've brought one of our upperclassmen from school!

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.190
Ta-da!

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:33.910
She's the Gardening Club's president, Mizushima Aya.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:40.600
I-It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.420
Um... no.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.130
Huh?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.180
That's Lord Coupe!

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.380
Huh? Lord Coupe?

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.140
Look!

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.220
My grandmother's over here.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.430
I'm really sorry about that! {Changed 'this' to 'that,' so it sounds a bit more natural in English.}

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:00.600
It's quite all right. No need to be so tense.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:05.190
She's nervous because she 
admires you so much, that's all. {Old: 'She's nervous cause she's meeting Tsubomi's oh-so-revered grandmother, that's all.' We'll assume the subject is taken.}

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:08.820
Aya has some things she wants to ask you about, apparently.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.280
I'll help as best I can.

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:15.160
Thank you very much!

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.240
What do you think about her?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.080
Do you sense anything about her?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.080
I'm not shure...

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:29.300
I'm always careful with my soil ratios and drainage, but somehow I just can't seem to raise flowers well.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:30.950
And?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:35.580
If there really are people in this world with a green thumb and without,

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.960
I'm sure I'm fall into the latter.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:42.940
So I was hoping you'd be able to give me some advice on where I'm going wrong!

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.400
Don't you get fed up with this?

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.370
Huh?

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.360
Grandma?

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.740
"Why do I keep messing up?" Don't you get 
fed up with always looking at your failures? {Do you not -> Don't you}

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.200
Look around you.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.700
This world is packed full of so many beautiful things.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:02.250
And yet, you choose not to enjoy all the wonders the world has to offer.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.210
Don't you think that's a waste?

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:07.710
Yes.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.650
All life is wonderful.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:14.640
But raising that life is always the hard part.

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:17.850
It's not something you can jump right into and just magically be good at.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:21.060
So whether you have a green thumb or not is irrelevant.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:26.520
What's important is to give them a lot of love and a lot of time.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.530
A lot of love and a lot of time...

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.340
I'm sure you'll do just fine.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:34.990
So have a little confidence.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.300
Thank you so much!

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.220
I won't be so negative anymore!{Literally just "I won't complain any more." but sounds dumb in English}{as much as I love 'emotastic', I think this is too awesome and serious a scene to dick around with. <3 Remind me to screencap it for the blag release thread, though.}

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:44.950
That's great, Aya! {Erika's pose: TITS}

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:46.000
Yeah...

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:51.170
Thanks to you, I got to hear some great words of advice from Grandma.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.110
Don't cry!

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.560
Good morning!

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:04.890
Aya, how are the flowers doing?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:10.610
They're still not doing great, but I'll take my time and be patient with them.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.010
Good morning, everyone!

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:12.740
Hm?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.200
Itsuki!

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:20.120
I'm sorry to intrude like this, but I have a favor to ask of the Gardening Club.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.790
Sure! What can we do for you?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:26.420
Well, the student council is proposing that we install some green curtains.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.500
I'd like to ask you to help us test if it's really viable.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.340
What's a "green curtain"?

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:37.340
It's a "curtain" made of plants that'll shade the 
windows from the bright sunlight during the summer.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.140
You really know your stuff, Hanasaki!

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.680
Oh, not at all...

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:46.890
If the experiment with the Gardening Club works out, we'll set them up all around the school next year.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.860
If that's what you're after, we'd be glad to help!

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.590
Thank you!

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.950
Our plants should arrive by the time school finishes today. {finished -> finishes, come on now.}

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:55.150
I'll leave it to you!

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:56.650
Okay!

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:05.620
If we grow these out, we should be able to cover both the windows in this classroom entirely.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:09.080
Let's give this all we've got, everyone!

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:10.750
Right!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.260
The green curtain is complete! {Holy shit, I didn't notice the implied TIMESKIP when watching this the first time.}

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.230
How wonderful!

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:29.940
Looks like covering the school in these next year should be very possible!

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:32.020
We did it, President!

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.940
And the seedlings you planted
 have all grown beautifully, Aya!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.910
All that stuff about you being bad at raising plants must've been your imagination!

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:43.670
Yeah, but it's all because you guys helped me out.

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:44.780
Thank you!

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:48.220
What's going on?!

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.080
They did say on the weather forecast that a typhoon would be passing nearby...

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:52.790
Huh?! A typhoon?!

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.880
Will the plants be all right? 
We only just arranged the buds.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.940
I'm burning... I'm burning up!

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:10.020
O' typhoon, rage more, and scatter these plants to the winds!

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:13.690
A new dawn beckons for the Desert Apostles!

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.660
I've had an epiphany!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.080
My new finisher shall be...

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:26.990
this!

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.710
A typhoon for a typhoon.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:36.870
With this Typhoon Punch, the Precure and that accursed third fairy...

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.920
shall fall!

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:57.470
Tsubomi!

00:11:58.490 --> 00:11:59.370
Erika!

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.200
School's canceled for the day cause of the typhoon.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:05.650
I know, but the green curtain...

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:07.170
You're worried about it, right?

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.440
I'm worried too!

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.920
That's why I can't let you go on your own, Tsubomi!

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:14.630
Erika...

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.220
Come on, let's go!

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:16.920
Right!

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.260
Aya!

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.170
Hanasaki, Kurumi!

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.260
At this rate, the vines are all going to untwine! {branches -> vines}

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.410
Let's set up a tarp to protect it! {net -> tarp because THAT IS NO NET}

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.060
Right!

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:40.690
Are you okay?!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:41.650
Yeah!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.150
Just a little bit more! Give it your all!

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.580
Okay!

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:47.650
Aya seems different today.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.870
Yeah, she really seems more reliable than before!

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.500
I wonder why...

00:12:57.030 --> 00:13:00.170
When I look at them, courage seems to flow through me!

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.720
Aya...

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.480
She has both kindness and strength!

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:06.140
She's a shweet girl!

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:07.690
We did it!

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:08.850
It's all set up!

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:12.110
And the wind seems to be dying down too.

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:14.020
We should be all right now, shouldn't we?

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:15.250
Yeah.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:18.560
<i>It's wilted...</i>

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:21.030
<i>The bud that I planted... {That's no bud, it's a vine!}{Yes, then it grew. When she planted it, it was a bud. ;o}</i>

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.860
That's perfect!

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.590
We did it, Aya!

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:32.000
Huh?

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.550
Aya?

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.080
Hey! {Oi -> Hey. Oi is a bit too British blah blah}{Actually, it's a bit Japanese.}

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:36.540
Itsuki!

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:40.400
You were all worried about the green curtain too, huh?

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:41.420
Itsuki!

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:44.090
Aya's gone.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:52.030
Why is that every plant I touch ends up dying?

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:53.710
<i>Hrm?</i>

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:58.190
The Flower of your Heart is wilting nicely.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:02.110
Flower of the Heart, show yourself!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:14.040
Very well. We shall make use of this today.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:18.250
You're up, Desertrian!

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.630
Bitter melon!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:27.390
Everyone, get out of here!

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.450
Thish ish bad!

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:37.090
Huh?

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.190
Aya's Flower of the Heart is the one...

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.690
...that was stolen!

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.860
Bitter melon!

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.030
Pleashe, hurry and shave her!

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:47.240
Right!

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:00.930
Go forth, Seeds of the Precure!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.310
Precure!

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:06.880
Open My Heart!

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:54.590
A lone flower, blooming from the earth!

00:15:57.990 --> 00:15:59.700
Cure Blossom!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:05.360
A lone flower, swaying in the sea breeze!

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.810
Cure Marine!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.090
HeartCatch Precure!

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:26.750
I love plants so much, so why am I no good at raising at them?!

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.040
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:32.120
You did raise them well!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:32.590
Look!

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:35.000
Wha—?!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.550
Why?!

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:40.180
I put so much love into them, yet this happened!

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:45.400
Aya...

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.900
Bitter melon!

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:51.900
Excellent work, Desertrian!

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.820
We shall ruin all plant life in this world...

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:59.530
and then reduce the hearts of 
people to the driest of deserts!

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.650
We won't allow it!

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:06.210
Aya's heart is filled with her genuine love for plants!

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:10.300
You're just abusing her heart in 
order to make a Desertrian from it.

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:14.590
I've had it up to here with this!

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:18.600
And on top of that, you're using the very plants she loves in order to destroy other plants.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:22.980
My heart may be vaster than the sea, but this is as much as it can take!

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:27.320
Desertrian! I shall leave you to defeat Cure Marine!

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:29.650
Bitter melon!

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:31.380
Marine!

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.930
Fear not. Because your opponent...

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:36.030
shall be me! {Look at the size of his damn fists. They're bigger than his head. FORESHORTENING!}

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:38.450
Take this!

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:41.370
Typhoon Punch!

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:44.830
Blossom!

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.750
Bitter melon!

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:58.800
Gather, Floral Power!

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:02.430
Marine Tact!

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.150
Flowers, glitter bright!

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:21.390
Precure Blue Forte Wave!

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.270
This is the end for you!

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:54.730
I'll put all the strength from the Flower of my Heart into my fist!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.860
Typhoon Punch!

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:01.030
Blossom Screw Punch!

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:12.630
Hmph.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.510
It seems we shall have to settle this another time.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:19.410
Things are finally getting interesting.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.300
Blossom!

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:24.420
Marine's got the Flower of her Heart!

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:26.060
She recovered it for us!

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.690
Thank goodness!

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.350
You guys!

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:41.240
Did something happen to Mizushima?

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.740
Oh, she's all right!

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:46.660
I think she's just exhausted 
because she was working so hard.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.290
I see...

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:49.370
Huh?

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:54.460
It's... it's so cute!

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.320
<i>What'sh with thish warmth I feel?</i>

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:01.680
<i>Could thish girl be the third Precure?</i>

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.670
U-Um...

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.640
We'll leave the rest to you.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:09.450
Very well.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.490
Aya!

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:20.520
Everyone...

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:23.360
When I saw that the seedling had withered like that... {added 'that' and 'had'}

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:25.320
You can still save it!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:26.280
Huh?

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:28.490
Here, take a look.

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:34.550
Some of the tendrils are still alive and growing well.

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:37.500
I'm sure the seedling is going to do just fine.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.070
You're right.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.690
And yet I just gave in to my despair and gave up on them so quickly.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:43.680
I'm sorry.

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:49.890
From now on, I'm going to raise you with a lot of love and give you a lot of time.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:03.700
I feel like the flowers are saying "Thank you" to her.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:05.540
Huh?!

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:07.760
No... I mustn't cry!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:11.480
From now on, I've got to be 
strong and care for my plants!

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:12.370
Right!

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:16.000
Aya, I think you're strong enough already.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:22.380
Don't they always say "Adversity builds character"?

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:25.990
In the language of flowers, a
 sasanqua means "genuine love."

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:30.600
Aya has genuine love for plants and the strength to protect them!

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:36.440
I think a Heart Seed's about to be born.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:51.270
With this, the Great Heart Tree has recovered a little more!

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:09.920
{ED}

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:18.810
HeartCatch!

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:21.730
HeartCatch!

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:24.650
HeartCatch!

00:22:24.940 --> 00:22:27.610
HeartCatch Precure!

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:36.160
The flower blooms with an "Open sesame!"

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:39.120
In the wardrobe of my heart

00:22:39.670 --> 00:22:42.290
are all the things that a girl loves

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:44.750
Look, they're packed in so tight

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:48.130
My makeover was a huge success

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:50.720
thanks to this scrunchie and this frilly tunic!

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:53.720
Our girly showtime

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:56.560
is about to begin!

00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:59.770
Is my coordination lookin' good today?

00:22:59.890 --> 00:23:02.690
Shuffle! Colorful! Beautiful!

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:05.610
Mismatches are just part of my character v(^^)v

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:07.150
We're pretty

00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:08.950
at full bloom!

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:12.070
If you polish your heart

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:15.120
until it shines

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:16.660
Then even the darkness

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:20.910
will become a guiding light

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:23.920
So don't sulk

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:26.840
because a smile's the best!

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:30.300
Let's make them bloom, facing the sun

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:33.510
The flowers of our hearts

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:36.390
HeartCatch!

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.890
HeartCatch Precure!

00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:45.230
<i>I've finally found my partner!</i>

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:47.320
<i>With eyes and hair of sparkling gold...</i>

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:49.600
<i>...and shining golden ribbons and frills!</i>

00:23:49.600 --> 00:23:51.670
<i>And beauty shurpasshing Venus hershelf!</i>

00:23:51.670 --> 00:23:53.660
<i>The strength to protect those she holds dear...</i>

00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:55.700
<i>...and bearing a heart full of burning justice!</i>

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:57.860
<i>Shining bright, like the Sun in the sky!</i>

00:23:57.860 --> 00:23:59.540
<i>Introducing our third member...</i>

00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:02.360
<i>Cure Sunshine!</i>

00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:04.130
HeartCatch Precure<i>:</i>

00:24:04.130 --> 00:24:06.590
Cure Sunshine

00:24:04.130 --> 00:24:06.590
Cure Sunshine

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:08.890
<i>We'll catch everyone's hearts!</i>
